hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28002","Narrated Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah, nephew of Amrah, I heard it from him before Az-Zuhri came, from a woman of the Ansar, she said: Our oven and the oven of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were one, and I did not memorize Qaf except from him, he used to recite it."
"28003","Narrated Yaqub, narrated my father, from Ibn Ishaq, narrated Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah, from Umm Hisham bint Harithah, she said: Our oven and the oven of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were one for two years, or a year and part of a year, and I did not learn Qaf and the Glorious Quran except from the tongue of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to recite it every Friday on the pulpit when he addressed the people."
"28180","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Man, on the authority of the daughter of Harithah ibn al-Numan, she said: I did not memorize Qaf except from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he preached on Friday. She said: And our oven and the oven of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were one."
"28181","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, and I heard it myself from al-Hakam, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said mentioned it, on the authority of Amrah, on the authority of Umm Hisham bint Harithah ibn al-Numan, she said: I did not take Qaf and the Glorious Quran except from behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to pray with it in the morning."
